            <div xml:id="d275">

                <pb facs="0367" n="265" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg265"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6127: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Tientsin (Lockhart) to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tientsin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-01T13:00:00+08:00">April 1, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 1—4:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Telegraphic reports from two reliable sources Chinwangtao state that Japanese
                    occupied Hsimenchai this morning, short distance north <pb facs="0368" n="266"
                        xml:id="pg266"/> of Chinwangtao and well inside the Wall. The situation in
                    region of Shanhaikwan is becoming more tense, considerable fighting west and
                    northwest that place having occurred. Japanese planes have been engaged in
                    reconnoitring that region for several days and in some instances dropping
                    bombs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
